    "body": "By Charlotte Goldstone\n1 November 2026\nHow reliable is container shipping right now, and what are the biggest factors impacting on-time performance?\nThis week on News in Brief, Xeneta Chief Analyst Peter Sand joins us to unpack the latest schedule reliability data, explore how different carrier alliance strategies are performing, and examine the ongoing impact of port congestion on capacity and sailing schedules.\nWe also discuss the proposed delay to US port fees on China-linked vessels, what it means for shippers, and take a look at the latest rate trends as the market heads out of Golden week and towards the Thanksgiving and Christmas peak season.\nWatch the episode on YouTube and subscribe so you never miss an update!\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xt1T_ZjGpmg&feature=youtu.be\nClick here to receive an email notification every time we release a podcast.\nThis article is © The Loadstar. Reproduction, rewriting, or derivative use requires a license. Contact [email protected] for licensing enquiries.",
